u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3. VALUATION (ENGINE 3 + ENGINE 4 CROSS-CHECK)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nENGINE SELECTION (Layer 0):\n  Archetype D: Product-Platform Hybrid. Reasons:\n   1. Hardware (product revenue $577M Q1 FY27) + installed-base monetization (sub ARR $2.0B).\n   2. Subscription revenue 45% of total, but product still >50% of revenue.\n   3. Transitioning toward Platform/Quality Compounder \u2014 NOT yet there (GAAP ROIC < WACC, FCF\n      positive but SBC-adjusted FCF razor-thin). Transition criteria: FCF+ for 2 consecutive\n      years on SBC-adjusted basis = NOT MET (FY25 0.106, FY26 0.134 \u2014 only 1 of 2; FY24 0.152).\n      \u21d2 BLENDED: Engine 3 primary; Engine 4 reverse-DCF as discipline. Conviction \u22120.5.\n\nENGINE 3 \u2014 CORE + PLATFORM PREMIUM [all B$, fiscal year]:\n  Forecast horizon FY27\u2013FY31. Explicit drivers:\n\n  FY27E Revenue 4.46 (guidance mid $4.41\u20134.51) [Actual guidance]\n       GP margin 68.5% [Assumption, Q1 68.7 actual]\n       Non-GAAP OI 0.84 (guidance $820\u2013860M) [Actual guidance] = 18.8% [Arithmetic]\n       SBC 12.5% rev = 0.56 [Assumption \u2014 history 12\u201314%]\n       Amort 0.031; D&A 0.178; Capex 0.290; \u0394WC 0.027 [Assumption]\n       GAAP OI = 0.84 \u2212 0.56 \u2212 0.03 = 0.25 [Arithmetic]\n       Cash tax 5% (NOLs) [Assumption]\n       AdjFCF = 0.25\u00d70.95 + 0.178 + 0.03\u00d70.95 \u2212 0.290 \u2212 0.027 = 0.13\n\n  FY28E Revenue 5.19 (+16.4%) [Assumption: hyperscaler lumpiness, enterprise digestion]\n       Non-GAAP OI 20.0% = 1.04 [Assumption: scale leverage, mix]\n   