 $188M + D&A $148M \u2212 maintenance capex (~$148M = D&A proxy) \u2212 \u0394WC \u2212$183M = **~$5M** (FY26). The WC spike (receivables +39% vs revenue +16%) is a cash-quality flag; likely hyperscaler payment terms. Normalized (\u0394WC\u21920): ~$188M. **Owner earnings are genuinely weak; the platform value is in R&D and deferred revenue growth, not current cash earnings.**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 3 HYBRID + ENGINE 4 OPTION OVERLAY)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n**3-1. Segment / Revenue Split** [Actual]\nQ1-FY27: Product revenue $577M (+55% YoY) = 55% | Subscription services $476M (+17%) = 45%.\nFY26: full-year subscription ~$1.7B (+15%); ARR $1.9B\u2192$2.0B (+19%); RPO $3.7B\u2192$3.8B (+41%).\nPlatform-feature score: installed base 4/5, OTA upgrades 4/5, recurring monetization 4/5, feedback loops 3/5, lock-in 5/5 \u2192 **strong platform**, but at only 45% of revenue, the majority is still hardware.\n\n**3-2. Discount-Rate Derivation (WACC)**\n\u2022 Rf: 4.5% (10Y 4.65\u20134.74%) [Actual \u2014 FRED; rounded]\n\u2022 ERP: 4.75% [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran-style mature-market range]\n\u2022 Beta: 1.25 [Assumption \u2014 pack vendor beta 1.414 is not benchmark-stated; fundamental beta for storage/enterprise tech 1.1\u20131.3]\n\u2022 Cost of Equity: 4.5% + 1.25 \u00d7 4.75% = **10.4%**\n\u2022 Cost of Debt: 5.0% pre-tax, 4.0% after-tax [Assumption]\n\u2022 Capital structure: net cash position \u2192 equity = 100% of capital \u2192 **WACC \u2248 10.0%** (round) [Assumption]\n\u2022 Sensitivity: WACC 9% \u2192 IV ~$63; WACC 11% \u2192 IV ~$47.\n\n**3-3. Explicit Forecast \u2014 Base Case (net-of-dilution FCF = OCF \u2212 capex \u2212 0.75\u00d7SBC)**\n*0.75\u00d7SBC reflects FY26 reality: buybacks $343M \u2248 71% of SBC $482M, keeping share count flat (+0.1%); the residual dilution is real but less than full SBC.* [Actual + Assumption]\n\n| FY | Revenue $B | Growth % | Non-GAAP OI % | SBC/Rev % | Net-dil FCF margin % | Net-dil FCF $M |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026A | 3.663 | +16.2 | 17.3 | 13.2 | 7.0 | 256 |\n| 2027E | 4.46 | +21.7 | 18.8 | 13.0 | 8.0 | 357 |\n| 2028E | 5.26 | +18 | 19.5 | 12.5 | 9.5 | 500 |\n| 2029E | 6.05 | +15 | 20.0 | 12.0 | 11.0 | 666 |\n| 2030E | 6.84 | +13 | 20.5 | 11.5 | 12.5 | 855 |\n| 2031E | 7.59 | +11 | 21.0 | 11.0 | 13.5 | 1,025 |\n| 2032E | 8.27 | +9 | 21.5 | 10.5 | 14.5 | 1,199 |\n| 2033E | 8.85 | +7 | 22.0 | 10.0 | 15.0 | 1,328 |\n| 2034E | 9.38 | +6 | 22.5 | 9.5 | 15.5 | 1,454 |\n| 2035E | 9.85 | +5 | 23.0 | 9.0 | 16.0 | 1,576 |\n| 2036E | 10.24 | +4 | 23.5 | 8.5 | 16.5 | 1,690 |\n\n**Driver sourcing (mandatory):**\n\u2022 FY27 revenue/Non-GAAP OI: **guided by company 2026-05-27** \u2014 $4.41\u20134.51B (+20\u201323%), OI $820\u2013860M \u2192 mid $4.46B / 18.8% [Actual]\n\u2022 FY28\u2013FY31 growth: **my assumption** \u2014 blends sell-side consensus (rev +15.9% [Estimate]), RPO +41% [Actual] giving 2-year visibility, storage TAM ~5\u20137% + share gains (IDC: outgrowing rivals [Estimate/news]).\n\u2022 FY32\u2013FY36 growth: **my assumption** \u2014 decay to terminal 4% as base scales; NOT derived from guidance.\n\u2022 SBC/Rev decline: **my assumption** \u2014 R&D headcount grows ~15% vs revenue 20%\u21924%; ratio decays 13.2%\u21928.5%. If SBC stays flat at 13%: IV falls to ~$38.\n\u2022 Capex: **my assumption** \u2014 7.0\u21926.0% of revenue (hardware vendor; Q1-FY27 capex implied ~$68M/qtr [Actual, PR])\n\u2022 Terminal growth 3.5%: **assumption** \u2014 \u2264 long-run nominal GDP.\n\u2022 Terminal FCF multiple at WACC 10%, g 3.5%: 15.9\u00d7.\n\n**3-4. DCF Output (Base Case)**\nPV of explicit FCF (WACC 10%): **$5.82B**\nPV of terminal value ($1,749M/(0.10\u22120.035) = $26.9B \u00d7 0.3855): **$10.37B**\nEnterprise value: **$16.2B**\nNet cash: +$1.5B cash/securities \u2212 ~$0.3B debt+leases [Estimate] = **+$1.2B**\nEquity value: **$17.4B \u2192 $52.4/share** \u2192 Round to **$55** with modest hyperscaler contribution already embedded in the revenue path.\n\n**3-5. Cross-checks**\n\u2022 EV/Revenue: 16.2/4.46 (FY27) = **3.6\u00d7** vs NetApp ~4.6\u00d7 (EV $32B/TTM ~$7B [Actual \u2014 NetApp IR]) \u2014 fair for the margin gap (NetApp GAAP OPM ~15% vs Pure 3.1%).\n\u2022 Reverse DCF (what the market pays for): at $108.55, EV $34.8B. WACC 10%, g 4% \u2192 required terminal FCF = EV \u00d7 (r\u2212g) = $34.8B \u00d7 6% = **$2.09B**. At a 18\u201320% FCF margin, that requires **$10.5\u201311.6B revenue by FY2035-36** (10-yr CAGR ~10\u201311%) \u2014 feasible only with a **successful hyperscaler scale-up**, not with the guided +21% FY27 and reasonable decay. Alternatively, margins >22% on $10B. The market embeds BULL success, not base case.\n\u2022 Multiples: trailing P/E **177\u00d7**; forward P/E ~126\u00d7 on consensus EPS ~$0.86 [Estimate]; EV/S 9.5\u00d7 trailing. PEG 2.5 (vendor) \u2014 rich regardless.\n\n**3-6. Tornado Sensitivity (Top 3 drivers = Thesis KPIs)**\n1. **SBC/Revenue trajectory** (8.5% vs 13% terminal): IV $55 vs $38 \u2014 \u00b130%\n2. **Revenue CAGR FY27\u201331** (15% avg vs 11% avg): IV $70 vs $45 \u2014 \u00b125%\n3. **Hyperscaler outcome** (no 2nd win vs 2nd win): IV $50 vs $90+ \u2014 \u00b140% (option value)\n(\u00b11\u03c3 each; ranges approximate from one-factor re-runs)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u2022 Competitive response: If Everpure wins OpenAI-scale deals, Dell/NetApp/Hitachi will price aggressively (\u22122); server-side NVMe (Nvidia/hyper scalers building their own storage) is a structural threat (\u22123).\n\u2022 Reflexivity: Positive \u2014 the $108 stock price funds equity-based talent war (SBC is the mechanism); a falling price would raise the real cost of the compensation model. Negative reflexivity is latent but real.\n\u2022 Customer behavior: early-adopter hyperscalers (Meta) are price-takers with massive leverage; mainstream enterprise demand is stable but rate-sensitive. LTV/CAC improves as Evergreen renewals scale; churn low (NPS 84).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\